From b1910949ed3566f3d92eecf2acb32b6f8b86d189 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:04:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: V2 service routes in the parity corpus

V2 records now request the V2 service's /v2 and /v2/explorer/v1 routes
(status, outpoint and branch queries, every explorer route with paging,
limit and malformed-input cases). The comparison parses JSON responses and
reports differing leaves. The per-process random service epoch, which also
appears in snapshot tokens and cursors, is zeroed on each side before
comparing; a response equal byte for byte after that is accepted as
"json.<service_epoch>". A Rust-vs-Rust V2 run (110 blocks, 13,493
requests) shows no other difference.

Tier: V2
---
